### Normalized scores (1–100)

> Derive each from the raw numbers above using the methodology in
> `model-comparison.md`. Add a one-sentence justification citing the key evidence,
> and state what caps it.
>
> **OVERALL SCORE FORMULA (v4, see `RULES.md`):**
> Overall = half-up mean of the five quality dims `(+ Reasoning + Context + Multimodal + Coding) / 5`.
> **NEVER include Cost efficiency** — scored independently.

- **Tool use: 70/100.** Based on strong performance on OSWorld (78.4%) and JobBench (75.3%), with moderate Terminal-Bench (57.1%) score; capped by lack of Tau3-Banking data.
- **Reasoning: 65/100.** Strong performance on AA-LCR (83.7%) but weak on Harvey LAB-AA (13.1%); average of all reasoning benchmarks caps this score.
- **Context window: 100/100.** 1M token context window places it in the top tier (≥1M = 95–100).
- **Multimodal: 90/100.** Supports text, image, video, and audio input, placing it in the +video/PDF in = 75–90 range.
- **Coding: 80/100.** Excellent DeepSWE score (79.0%) and strong ProgramBench (59.0%), with moderate SWE-Marathon (57.5%); capped by lack of SWE-bench Verified data.
- **Cost efficiency: 30/100.** Subscription-only model with no free tier available; significantly more expensive than pay-as-you-go alternatives.
- **Overall Score: 81/100.** Mean of tool (70), reasoning (65), context (100), multimodal (90), and coding (80) scores.

